@{
    Layout = "/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
    ViewData["Title"] = "About — Bitcoin Digital Objects (BDO)";

    // Presentation only: show the actually installed plugin version from the
    // assembly, instead of a hardcoded string. Falls back to "unknown" if the
    // assembly version is unavailable.
    var pluginVersion =
        typeof(BTCPayServer.Plugins.Smv.SmvPlugin).Assembly.GetName().Version?.ToString(3)
        ?? "unknown";
}

<section class="container my-4" style="max-width: 760px;">
    <header class="mb-4">
        <h1 class="mb-1">Bitcoin Digital Objects (BDO)</h1>
        <p class="text-muted mb-0">Reference implementation for STAS-01</p>
    </header>

    <partial name="_SmvPluginNav" />

    <p>
        Bitcoin Digital Objects (BDOs) are verifiable digital objects secured by Bitcoin. <strong>Bitcoin Digital Objects</strong> is the reference implementation for
        <strong>STAS-01</strong>, an open standard for issuing, signing, anchoring and
        verifying Bitcoin-native digital assets.
    </p>

    <p>
        Developed and maintained by Supermultiverse, this plugin lets BTCPay Server merchants
        <strong>create, hold, send, receive and verify</strong> Bitcoin Digital Objects —
        without leaving BTCPay.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-4">What this plugin does</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Create</strong> Bitcoin Digital Objects and mint them into a hosted wallet.</li>
        <li><strong>Manage</strong> the BDOs you hold, and move them out any time with <strong>Send</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Receive</strong> BDOs into a self-custody (BYON) wallet.</li>
        <li><strong>Verify</strong> any BDO against Bitcoin mainnet by ID — proof integrity, issuer
            signature and anchor data, validated independently.</li>
        <li><strong>Inspect</strong> Bitcoin mainnet anchor data via <code>mempool.space</code>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-4">STAS-01 Standard</h2>

    <p>
        STAS-01 defines how Bitcoin-native digital assets are:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Described through metadata.</li>
        <li>Signed by an issuer.</li>
        <li>Anchored to Bitcoin.</li>
        <li>Distributed together with proof files.</li>
        <li>Independently verified by third parties.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        Bitcoin Digital Objects implements the STAS-01 verification workflow and serves as
        the reference verifier for the standard.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-4">What is verified</h2>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>Proof integrity</strong> via SHA-256 against the issuer-published hash.</li>
        <li><strong>Issuer signature</strong> over the metadata hash.</li>
        <li><strong>Bitcoin anchor information</strong> including network and anchor outpoint.</li>
        <li><strong>Bitcoin Digital Object proof data</strong> downloadable for independent validation.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-4">Trust model</h2>

    <p>
        Verification ultimately relies on Bitcoin mainnet data and cryptographic proofs.
        APIs act only as distribution layers for publicly verifiable artifacts.
    </p>

    <p>
        The STAS-01 trust model does not require trust in Supermultiverse or any issuer.
        Once a proof has been downloaded, verification can be performed independently using
        the proof file, issuer signature and Bitcoin anchor data.
    </p>

    <p>
        In short:
    </p>

    <blockquote class="blockquote">
        <p class="mb-0">Don't trust. Verify.</p>
    </blockquote>

    <h2 class="mt-4">Open Standard</h2>

    <p>
        STAS-01 is the open and auditable specification designed for interoperability across
        Bitcoin-native digital asset ecosystems. Anyone may build compatible implementations
        against it.
    </p>

    <p>
        Bitcoin Digital Objects (BDOs) are the open category for Bitcoin-secured ownership.
        Supermultiverse provides the reference implementation and platform. The Supermultiverse
        platform itself is not open source.
    </p>

